WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:08.640
The 37th All-Foundation Combined Athletic Festival Competition...

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:09.620
...has finally begun!

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.500
This time, the second Foundation, the Stellvia, will be the arena.

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:13.440
Prayer for victory

00:00:12.650 --> 00:00:13.150
Fight like fury

00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:14.110
Victory will be ours!

00:00:13.590 --> 00:00:15.810
Each of the events have opened up with fierce competition.

00:00:16.910 --> 00:00:20.300
And the festival isn't being watched just by the schools...

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:21.650
...but by the entire world.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:24.680
There are some press people here from each planet participating...

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:28.380
...and we are being satellite broadcast to the entire Sol system.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars, Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:36.890
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて 飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
Carry the unexpierence of the heart in the hands and go far away

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:44.840
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて go far away

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
Urayamu koto ni Narete shimattara

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
If you have experienced the envy

00:00:55.860 --> 00:00:59.940
羨む事に 慣れてしまったら

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Hokoreru jibun ga Toozakatteku

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
Your proud self will go far away

00:01:02.340 --> 00:01:05.970
誇れる自分が 遠ざかってく

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Mienai tsubasa de habataku no fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
Flapping the invisible wings to fly higher

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:13.140
見えない翼で羽ばたくの fly higher

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
Yume wo egaku no wa hito ni umareta kara

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
I'm imaging dreams because I was born a "person"

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:20.470
夢を描くのは「人」に生まれたから

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Sora wo aogi Hoshi yo michite

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
Look up to the sky, rise to the stars,

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:24.580
空を仰ぎ 星よ満ちて

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Tobitatsu no Asu e no brilliant road

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
Take-off on the brilliant road of tomorrow.

00:01:24.580 --> 00:01:28.040
飛び立つの 明日への brilliant road

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Kokoro no aosa Kono te ni daite

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
Carry the unexperienced of the heart in the hands

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:32.920
心の蒼さ この手に抱いて

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
Anata to nara Yowai jibun wo sarakedashite hashiridaseru no

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
If I were with you, I'd start running, exposing my weak self

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:40.850
あなたとなら 弱い自分をさらけ出して走り出せるの

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
Mirai yo dou ka Mugen ni tsuzuke go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
The future! Somehow continues to the infinity, go far away

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:48.540
未来よどうか 無限に続け go far away

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:06.020
Episode Six:
I Won't Lose

00:02:02.600 --> 00:02:04.020
We are resuming our relay.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.550
Now then, reporting on the current state of the games...

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:09.600
According to the scores after the eighth event...

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:13.790
...our Stellvia team has managed to keep the top spot!

00:02:19.520 --> 00:02:24.980
And today, the main event, the first round of astroball, is going to begin!

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:27.670
The Stellvia Campus Broadcasting Club...

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:29.750
...will be reporting on the progress...

00:02:30.220 --> 00:02:32.870
...of the first match between the Stellvia team and the Vision team...

00:02:32.950 --> 00:02:35.510
...via a completely live broadcast, starting right now.

00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:37.970
Your presenters today will be the girl who shone...

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:40.110
...as the winner of the popularity contest, the newcomer...

00:02:40.190 --> 00:02:42.650
...who's a surprise to the Broadcasting Club, Arisa Glennorth...

00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.350
And the servant to all of the female students, Pierre Takida.

00:02:46.610 --> 00:02:47.800
What do you mean by that!?

00:02:48.230 --> 00:02:49.390
Oh! That's not what I mean!

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:52.950
The commentary will be done by the sweet and sour opinion duo...

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:56.660
...of Mr. Richard James and Mr. Carl Hutter.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:02:57.900
Thank you for coming.

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.550
Who's the sour one, who?

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:02.340
Now, now...

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:07.110
The units for both teams have entered the game field!

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.130
This competition takes place in a field that is enveloped by a barrier.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:21.980
Both teams have five Ora-avis machines...

00:03:21.980 --> 00:03:23.230
...moving their way through it...

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:25.420
...avoiding several obstacles floating in the field while manipulating...

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:28.460
...a ball that is only one meter in diameter via anti-gravity sticks.

00:03:28.460 --> 00:03:31.570
You compete by making shots in your opponent's goal and earning points.

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:33.800
It has an unusually high level of difficulty.

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.070
And now the game field has been enveloped.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.570
The match is about to begin!

00:03:54.690 --> 00:03:55.820
Hmm...
Hmm...

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.520
Go!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:03:59.690
Quickly get inside your opponent's formation!

00:03:58.410 --> 00:04:00.260
We can't see the screen!

00:03:59.930 --> 00:04:02.840
Whoever gets the ball first will win! Don't give any openings!

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.980
You're a teacher, so calm down a little more.

00:04:02.980 --> 00:04:04.490
Get the ball and keep attacking!

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:04.490
Oh, dear...

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.030
We're going to attack in one shot with four tops.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.880
Katase, you defend the goal with your life.

00:04:11.430 --> 00:04:12.640
Don't leave the goal!

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:13.590
Roger.

00:04:13.710 --> 00:04:14.310
Roger.

00:04:14.870 --> 00:04:15.640
Acknowledged.

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:18.810
Katase?

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:21.050
Y-yes! I understand!

00:04:21.430 --> 00:04:23.570
Katase, relax, relax.

00:04:24.180 --> 00:04:25.880
If you do it just like we practiced, it'll be fine.

00:04:26.170 --> 00:04:27.850
Right! I'll do my best!

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:38.170
And the match begins! The Vision team has the ball first!

00:04:41.010 --> 00:04:42.100
Let's go get the ball!

00:04:42.680 --> 00:04:43.840
Ayaka, put the pressure on them.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.580
Syoujin, you're backup!

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:46.940
Roger.
Acknowledged.

00:04:47.910 --> 00:04:51.500
Machida and Syoujin aggressively going after the ball.

00:04:51.850 --> 00:04:56.350
Austin and Gebourg are guarding the other players and closing the gap.

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.590
And Katase is...

00:05:02.960 --> 00:05:05.330
Oh! She's stopped?

00:05:05.730 --> 00:05:07.160
Eh? Huh?

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:08.510
What?

00:05:08.840 --> 00:05:10.760
Miss Katase, defend the goal!

00:05:10.790 --> 00:05:13.630
Oh, yes. I mean, roger!

00:05:21.200 --> 00:05:24.920
It appears as if Miss Katase is nervous about her first time on the field.

00:05:25.220 --> 00:05:27.850
Do your best, Shipon! Don't lose!

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.250
Hey, you, be a little more composed.

00:05:33.320 --> 00:05:33.920
Oh, no!

00:05:36.760 --> 00:05:38.750
Miss Katase, the ball's heading your way!

00:05:38.830 --> 00:05:40.030
Oh, right...

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.140
Take that!

00:05:50.980 --> 00:05:51.500
What?

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:52.140
What?

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:53.010
What?

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:56.020
What?

00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.540
What are you, stupid!?

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.260
Eh? Now what?

00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:06.510
Shipon?

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.860
She touched an obstacle, didn't she?

00:06:10.190 --> 00:06:11.460
So it seems.

00:06:11.980 --> 00:06:14.350
Which means... according to the rules...?

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:17.820
Ejection from the field.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.470
No way...

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:20.830
Shipon...

00:06:26.230 --> 00:06:28.200
In one sense, this might just be exciting.

00:06:28.920 --> 00:06:30.630
Katase, ejected.

00:06:30.630 --> 00:06:33.060
Huh? Ejected? What?

00:06:31.090 --> 00:06:34.590
Katase, ejected. Katase, ejected.

00:06:41.500 --> 00:06:43.130
Okonomiyaki

00:06:51.360 --> 00:06:53.100
Don't be so down.

00:06:53.560 --> 00:06:56.310
They won the match even without you, Shipon.

00:06:56.680 --> 00:06:57.470
That's right...

00:06:57.870 --> 00:07:00.210
And being ejected from the field in thirty seconds is a record.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:02.010
It's a record!

00:07:02.270 --> 00:07:05.820
That's not praise...

00:07:05.940 --> 00:07:09.620
Stop using that sad voice, because it's scary.

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:14.180
In the first place, why are you ejected in one shot just for touching it a little?

00:07:14.500 --> 00:07:16.690
Well, that's because astroball is a sport that came from a competition...

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:21.030
...involving controlling one's ship in an area of space...

00:07:21.440 --> 00:07:22.510
...that had lots of obstacles, isn't it?

00:07:22.820 --> 00:07:23.600
Jojo...

00:07:23.920 --> 00:07:26.210
Are you having a teething fever or something?

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:27.570
Jeez, you guys...

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.100
All you have to do is do your best at the next match.

00:07:32.400 --> 00:07:33.640
Otoyama...

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:38.440
Yes, yes, thank you very much for that.

00:07:38.560 --> 00:07:40.610
Could it be that we're intruding?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:42.460
One, two...

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:43.990
There we go!

00:07:45.380 --> 00:07:46.850
Whoa! It's huge!

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.820
Sauce and mayonnaise, drip drip.

00:07:51.020 --> 00:07:53.100
Green dried seaweed and bonito flakes... shake shake.

00:07:53.470 --> 00:07:54.840
It's very well done...

00:07:55.070 --> 00:07:57.830
Now cut, cut, cut, and...

00:08:00.100 --> 00:08:00.680
Here you are...

00:08:01.140 --> 00:08:02.120
It's ready to eat.

00:08:07.010 --> 00:08:09.070
Now, eat this and cheer up...

00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:11.750
...and do your best tomorrow, Shipon.

00:08:12.970 --> 00:08:13.750
Yeah...

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:19.280
Thank you, Yayoi. Thank you, everyone.

00:08:19.790 --> 00:08:21.790
Shima Katase is going to do her best!

00:08:21.960 --> 00:08:23.720
All right, do your best!

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:24.450
Hot hot hot!

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.160
That was fast, Arisa.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:29.830
Welcome!

00:08:29.900 --> 00:08:32.340
Is "okonomiyaki" really tasty?

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:34.220
I told you, it'll be all right.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:39.080
Oh, it's the ejected girl.

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:40.180
Really?

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.350
Oh, she's cute!

00:08:42.690 --> 00:08:44.400
Could it be that you're... fans?

00:08:44.630 --> 00:08:47.380
You see, you're a star, aren't you?

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:48.450
Dummy...
Huh?

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.470
Those are our next opponents.

00:08:50.620 --> 00:08:51.220
What?

00:08:51.340 --> 00:08:52.250
Take a good look.

00:08:52.810 --> 00:08:54.350
They're the representative team for the Odyssey...

00:08:54.780 --> 00:08:56.290
...who beat the Akapusu team in the first round.

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:59.930
But when they're piloting the Ora-avis machines, you can't see their faces.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:01.780
Wouldn't you normally look at the player list?

00:09:02.670 --> 00:09:05.940
Well, the Akapusu team didn't really respond, either...

00:09:06.120 --> 00:09:08.310
...so it feels like it'll be an easy victory over the Stellvia team.

00:09:08.310 --> 00:09:09.210
What did you say!?

00:09:09.560 --> 00:09:11.740
You play astroball with five players.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:16.380
If someone gets ejected quickly, like she did, then it's not much of a match.

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.470
We won today!

00:09:19.620 --> 00:09:21.620
That's right, you tell them, Shipon!

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:24.480
They worked hard at defense, and won 1-0, though.

00:09:25.170 --> 00:09:26.730
This isn't soccer, you know.

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.020
Something like that won't work on us.

00:09:29.130 --> 00:09:30.460
That's not it at all!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:33.490
Don't deal with low level people.

00:09:37.260 --> 00:09:38.990
Tell this to Austin and the others.

00:09:39.600 --> 00:09:41.740
Tell them, "don't get too carried away by flattering yourselves...

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:43.710
...saying you're the Big Four."

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.840
Aren't you the ones getting carried away?

00:09:49.900 --> 00:09:50.530
Humph!

00:09:55.270 --> 00:09:57.620
What do you mean, young miss?

00:09:59.290 --> 00:10:01.900
She caught a ball going over 300 kilometers per hour squarely...

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.050
...without trapping it, and sent it back.

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:07.290
And she did it in a training Bianca.

00:10:08.030 --> 00:10:11.730
How many people are there in your group that can pull that trick off?

00:10:11.960 --> 00:10:12.620
What?

00:10:15.860 --> 00:10:19.040
Shipon was chosen as a player because of her own skills.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:21.820
If you think of her as weak, you'll end up having a painful experience.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:25.140
Captain!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.310
I've lost my desire to have fun.

00:10:29.720 --> 00:10:30.750
Um...

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:37.200
I won't lose.

00:10:37.550 --> 00:10:40.440
Tomorrow, I definitely will not lose to all of you.

00:10:42.090 --> 00:10:43.040
Let's meet on the field.

00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:53.310
And who are you?

00:10:54.090 --> 00:10:55.640
I'm Rinna Kazamatsuri.

00:10:56.350 --> 00:10:57.160
Nice to meet you.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:33.360
So you came over from the Ultima, Miss Kazamatsuri?

00:11:33.760 --> 00:11:34.620
Isn't that scary?

00:11:34.980 --> 00:11:39.550
It's not complete there, but it's the closest to the Second Wave, isn't it?

00:11:39.810 --> 00:11:42.810
Right. The frontline base for the continuation of humanity.

00:11:43.420 --> 00:11:44.950
That's why it's a hot place.

00:11:45.240 --> 00:11:45.910
A hot place...?

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:50.450
What are you guys doing at a time like this?

00:11:51.000 --> 00:11:51.460
Ack!

00:11:53.400 --> 00:11:54.100
This is bad!

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.950
It's no use running now. Jeez!

00:11:57.300 --> 00:12:00.600
Now, now... this time we'll let it slide.

00:12:00.890 --> 00:12:01.440
Bad boy!

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:03.720
What an enjoyable scolding.

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:05.490
Want me to scold you, too?

00:12:05.490 --> 00:12:07.010
N-no, that was enough!

00:12:07.360 --> 00:12:08.610
Heya, Katase.
Huh?

00:12:09.220 --> 00:12:10.630
You were pretty flashy out there today.

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.220
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:15.660
This isn't class. You don't have to apologize.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:17.920
Be sure to make a comeback tomorrow.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:19.310
Huh...

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:21.940
That's a pretty vague answer.

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:24.020
Frank, you've got to be frank about it.

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:26.420
I-I'm sorry.

00:12:30.530 --> 00:12:34.600
Hey, Katase. Why do you want to be a pilot?

00:12:35.070 --> 00:12:35.590
What...?

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:40.140
You guys have been chosen to carry the burden...

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.950
...of being humanity's advance into the universe.

00:12:42.900 --> 00:12:44.650
You're going to represent all people...

00:12:45.250 --> 00:12:47.850
...and don't forget that that's why you're here.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:49.640
Y-yes, sir.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:52.940
All right. Be sure to play well tomorrow.

00:12:53.660 --> 00:12:54.470
You can do it.

00:12:55.050 --> 00:12:58.080
Show those Odyssey guys a rough time. Got it?

00:12:58.780 --> 00:13:00.660
Go! Go! Go!

00:13:01.030 --> 00:13:03.400
Nice fight! Let's fight! Fire!

00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:06.070
Huh...

00:13:07.570 --> 00:13:10.520
Whoa, he's really enthusiastic!

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.030
He's jealous of you all.

00:13:13.730 --> 00:13:14.750
Really?

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.380
I heard that Mr. Shirogane...

00:13:16.790 --> 00:13:19.910
...is next in line to be the leader of the Stellvia, but...

00:13:20.580 --> 00:13:22.900
He really wanted to be a pilot.

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:27.610
So try and live up to his hopes, students!

00:13:27.670 --> 00:13:30.530
Go! Go! Let's fight! Fire!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:38.000
The teachers on the Stellvia are kind of amusing.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:39.230
That's right...

00:13:39.380 --> 00:13:41.580
Doesn't it feel like they're enjoying their youth more than we are?

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:47.100
What'll I do? I have no self-confidence.

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:50.800
Wouldn't it be best for you to do what you do best, Shima-chan?

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.390
There's nothing else you can do, right?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:56.440
That's right.

00:13:56.790 --> 00:13:58.550
Well, the thing you should endeavor for...

00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:01.590
...is to not get ejected before the match ends.

00:14:01.850 --> 00:14:05.430
Oh, Arisa, you always say things like that so easily!

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:09.080
But putting forth your effort step by step is important, too.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:12.810
That's right, you're good at programming, Shipon...

00:14:13.040 --> 00:14:15.350
...so how about calculating the motion of everything?

00:14:15.490 --> 00:14:17.140
Yayoi!

00:14:21.020 --> 00:14:22.780
Go, go, Stellvia!

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:24.690
Let's fight! Nice fight!

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:34.200
And now it's finally time for the second round of astroball!

00:14:34.840 --> 00:14:35.970
The winners of this match...

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:40.100
...will go against the winners from two festivals ago, the El Santo team.

00:14:40.480 --> 00:14:43.750
Mr. James, does the Stellvia team have any chance of victory?

00:14:47.130 --> 00:14:49.530
I'd like for everyone to do their best...

00:14:51.870 --> 00:14:53.120
That was Mr. James!

00:14:59.960 --> 00:15:02.540
Fight, Shipon!

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:08.530
Oh, you've got quite a good place, don't you?

00:15:09.020 --> 00:15:09.770
Mr. Shirogane?

00:15:09.970 --> 00:15:11.480
Open up over there.

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:13.960
Why have you come all this way?

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.900
Who can watch this in the quiet teacher's room?

00:15:17.410 --> 00:15:19.230
If we're going to support our team, then it has to be here!

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:21.510
Saying that "it has to be here!"...

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:23.940
Beat the Odyssey! Now is the time to rise up! 

00:15:27.840 --> 00:15:32.180
The Ora-avis machines the players are piloting have entered the field.

00:15:32.860 --> 00:15:35.880
Mr. Hutter, what do you think of the condition of the Stellvia team?

00:15:36.660 --> 00:15:38.430
I believe that the abilities of each member...

00:15:38.500 --> 00:15:40.520
...are, of course, the best of all the teams, but...

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:41.260
But?

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:44.620
But Shima Katase, who was chosen from the preparatory students, is...

00:15:44.970 --> 00:15:46.580
Hmm... Katase is...

00:15:46.610 --> 00:15:47.710
Mr. Hutter!

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:51.340
To be honest, Katase has a lot of unknown factors to her...

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:55.030
Though it's good to possess individual talents...

00:15:55.950 --> 00:15:58.870
N-now, the field has been enveloped in the barrier.

00:15:59.390 --> 00:16:01.070
The match is about to begin!

00:16:10.410 --> 00:16:12.030
The formation is just like yesterday.

00:16:12.260 --> 00:16:14.140
Ayaka and Syoujin, you break through the front...

00:16:14.600 --> 00:16:16.310
...and Naji and I will pick up any fumbled balls.

00:16:16.770 --> 00:16:18.250
Katase, you defend the goal.

00:16:18.560 --> 00:16:20.870
Katase, just relax as you go. Okay?

00:16:21.600 --> 00:16:24.140
Miss Katase. Miss Katase, are you listening?

00:16:24.520 --> 00:16:26.720
Oh, yes. I'm all right.

00:16:27.120 --> 00:16:28.970
Today I will defend the goal to the last.

00:16:31.080 --> 00:16:32.620
The first ball goes to the Stellvia team.

00:16:44.040 --> 00:16:44.560
What?

00:16:46.470 --> 00:16:47.330
Well, now...

00:16:47.680 --> 00:16:49.480
...Machida's unit has been marked by two units, and she can't make a pass.

00:16:53.260 --> 00:16:53.930
Got it!

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:54.510
Tst.

00:16:55.170 --> 00:16:56.470
And now the ball has been intercepted...

00:16:56.710 --> 00:16:58.910
The ball has gone to the Odyssey team!

00:16:59.740 --> 00:17:02.340
Because Miss Machida was blocked in the front and the back...

00:17:02.890 --> 00:17:06.280
...she tried to use the wall to pass to Mister Syoujin, who was behind her...

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:10.350
...but that was accounted for, and the ball was skillfully stolen away.

00:17:10.530 --> 00:17:13.680
That's because Miss Machida is a key player for their attacks.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:19.690
If she isn't able to move, then Mister Austin has to come up to the front...

00:17:19.840 --> 00:17:22.170
And in that case, their defense will be short-handed.

00:17:22.670 --> 00:17:26.580
What is with that!? Isn't that against the rules?

00:17:26.810 --> 00:17:27.850
According to the rules...

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:30.860
...it's not illegal for two competing units to touch one another.

00:17:31.000 --> 00:17:35.480
Even still, it's certain to get them a warning for reckless playing.

00:17:35.830 --> 00:17:37.910
At worst, they were containing her movements...

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:41.080
...ready to be ejected from the game if it would take Miss Machida with them.

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.850
Are they that afraid of Machida?

00:17:44.970 --> 00:17:48.900
More likely, they probably think that little of Miss Katase.

00:17:49.190 --> 00:17:51.440
Look, they have two units on Miss Machida.

00:17:51.790 --> 00:17:53.500
Miss Katase is completely free.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:56.760
They're looking down on her!

00:17:57.490 --> 00:17:59.190
Hey, your persona is changing.

00:18:04.200 --> 00:18:05.470
If this is how it's going to be...

00:18:05.820 --> 00:18:09.910
...then I'll trace the movements of every object in the field!

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.070
Katase, it's coming your way.

00:18:13.330 --> 00:18:14.380
Roger!

00:18:18.510 --> 00:18:19.640
Rebound!

00:18:19.700 --> 00:18:20.220
Right!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:25.260
What!?

00:18:27.190 --> 00:18:28.280
Too bad!

00:18:28.750 --> 00:18:31.060
Umm... who can I pass to...?

00:18:33.810 --> 00:18:34.770
Not possible, huh?

00:18:35.250 --> 00:18:37.020
In that case... here I go!

00:18:45.620 --> 00:18:47.640
Th-this is incredible!

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:52.720
Katase is using every obstacle to rebound and move the ball forward!

00:18:52.980 --> 00:18:55.120
Go! Go! Shipon!

00:18:55.230 --> 00:18:57.550
Send those Odyssey guys flying!

00:18:57.560 --> 00:18:58.420
Hey, hey.

00:19:01.650 --> 00:19:07.350
Go! Fight! Fight! Shima! Shima! Let's go, Shipon!

00:19:07.780 --> 00:19:08.800
Amazing.

00:19:09.260 --> 00:19:12.180
Is she calculating the paths of everything out there?

00:19:12.760 --> 00:19:16.310
It can't be... she took what you said seriously, Milady.

00:19:16.950 --> 00:19:19.550
You can't do that in real time.

00:19:19.870 --> 00:19:22.280
No, this is Shipon, so...

00:19:22.710 --> 00:19:24.210
She probably is doing it.

00:19:24.350 --> 00:19:25.310
Are you serious?

00:19:26.150 --> 00:19:27.890
What are you doing? It's just one unit!

00:19:28.110 --> 00:19:30.220
Stop her! Interrupt the ball using all units!

00:19:30.280 --> 00:19:31.960
Her course is so complex, we can't follow it!

00:19:32.100 --> 00:19:32.940
Damn it!

00:19:37.680 --> 00:19:41.640
Weren't you supposed to be my opponents?

00:19:41.880 --> 00:19:44.640
Syoujin, Naji, give Miss Katase some support!

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:45.520
Roger!
 Acknowledged!

00:19:47.680 --> 00:19:48.540
Damn it!
 Damn it!

00:19:48.610 --> 00:19:49.640
We won't let you interfere!

00:19:49.770 --> 00:19:53.310
"Turn, hellhound, turn," from Macbeth.

00:19:58.160 --> 00:19:59.600
I won't let you get it in the goal.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.480
Go!

00:20:08.130 --> 00:20:09.460
W-what!?

00:20:14.960 --> 00:20:16.610
She did it, Katase made her first go...

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.530
Goal! Goal! Goal! Goal! Goal!

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.100
Shipon's first goal!

00:20:22.360 --> 00:20:23.340
Hey, you, Pierre is...

00:20:24.410 --> 00:20:27.830
But using the referee's unit to rebound off of...

00:20:27.830 --> 00:20:29.970
...that is honestly a very advanced intellectual play.

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:34.350
Seriously. I'd like for that insight to show up in class.

00:20:52.610 --> 00:20:54.780
I did it, everyone.

00:20:55.560 --> 00:20:56.950
Well done, Katase...

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:00.510
All right! Let's switch Katase and Ayaka to the two top positions!

00:21:01.050 --> 00:21:04.320
Syoujin, Naji, get the ball to Katase!

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:05.270
Roger!
 Acknowledged!

00:21:05.420 --> 00:21:08.890
All right! Here I come again!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.290
Beat the Odyssey! Now is the time to rise up! 

00:21:20.770 --> 00:21:21.770
I'm sorry, Rinna.

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:25.900
It's become so that I have to go back to the Ultima right away.

00:21:26.180 --> 00:21:27.670
Then let's hurry.

00:21:27.750 --> 00:21:30.720
You don't have to see me off. Watch the match until the end.

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:33.500
It's all right. The result is obvious.

00:21:33.840 --> 00:21:36.070
And I don't get to see you for a while, Papa.

00:21:36.440 --> 00:21:38.580
I see... did you have fun?

00:21:38.670 --> 00:21:39.050
Yea.

00:21:39.480 --> 00:21:40.930
And I made a friend.

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:42.400
That's good.

00:21:42.810 --> 00:21:46.330
She's an incredible person. Someone worthy of being my rival.

00:21:47.580 --> 00:21:52.380
Oh, and Katase has just gotten her third point!

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
Atashi wa itsumo sora wo Hikaru sora wo miageteta

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
I was always looking up at the sky, the sparkling sky

00:21:55.010 --> 00:22:00.540
あたしはいつも空を 光る空を見上げてた

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
Tabitatsu tsubasa te ni ire Kono sora mioroshite mitai no

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
I'll obtain wings to take off because I want to look down at this sky

00:22:01.620 --> 00:22:07.220
飛び立つ翼手に入れ この空見下ろしてみたいの

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Mirai wa dou agaitete mo Kanarazu otozureru kara

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
Even with how I'm struggling, I'll certainly visit the future

00:22:08.500 --> 00:22:14.980
未来はどうあがいてても 必ず訪れるから

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
Dare mo mita koto no nai keshiki wo Nozonde shimau

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
I'm wishing for scenery that no one has seen

00:22:15.110 --> 00:22:20.890
誰も見たことのない景色を 望んでしまう

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
Todomaru koto wo shiranai Fuan wo kakaeta yume wo

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
I don't know about things that stay put, or dreams that hold onto anxiety

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:28.670
とどまる事を知らない 不安を抱えた夢を

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Ima wa kokoro omomuku mama ni dakou

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
Now let's embrace the proceeding spirit

00:22:29.260 --> 00:22:35.590
今は心赴くままに抱こう

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
Naite warau tabi ni omou Atashi ga ikiteru imi wo

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
I cry every time I think you smile, I'll live for the meaning of it

00:22:35.940 --> 00:22:42.380
泣いて笑う度に思う あたしが生きてる意味を

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
Hito wa maru de Irotoridori no hoshi no you da ne

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
People are completely multicolored like the stars, you know?

00:22:42.510 --> 00:22:51.550
人はまるで 色とりどりの星のようだね

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
Kazaritateta you na kirei na yozora

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
The beautifully decked out night sky

00:22:52.160 --> 00:22:58.600
飾り立てたような綺麗な夜空

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
Soshite mata Atashi wa miageta

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
And still I looked up

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:04.510
そしてまた あたしは見上げた・・・

00:23:05.020 --> 00:23:07.030
Next episode

00:23:05.620 --> 00:23:06.210
This is Shima!

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:06.850
This is Arisa!

00:23:07.130 --> 00:23:09.850
Thanks to her actions at the athletic festival, Shipon is full of confidence!

00:23:09.850 --> 00:23:12.130
No, that's not it at all.

00:23:11.720 --> 00:23:14.500
And we begin a new kind of training.

00:23:14.560 --> 00:23:16.280
It's called the "Lightning Joust".

00:23:16.360 --> 00:23:19.050
You attach a spear to your Bianca, and fight with two crafts.

00:23:19.120 --> 00:23:22.420
And then, we have combined training with the regular upperclassmen...

00:23:22.490 --> 00:23:24.820
...but we won't lose to them, right?

00:23:24.830 --> 00:23:26.680
On the next episode of Stellvia of the Universe...

00:23:26.990 --> 00:23:28.030
"Frustration"

00:23:28.060 --> 00:23:29.160
Huh? What's that?

00:23:29.730 --> 00:23:32.710
Are you going to lose? Hey! Wait!

00:23:32.050 --> 00:23:35.010
Episode Seven:
Frustration

00:23:32.880 --> 00:23:34.180
Please look forward to it!
